findings=[
 {'id':'Q328','title':'Reopening the workshop library clears the embedding host export protections','source':'crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/src/state.rs:165,521,536; ports/pelt/desktop/appearance_editor.rs:67,127','status':'source-verified full current Workshop/Pelt caller chain; actual export overwrite and full Workshop runtime not executed','evidence':'set_protected_export_paths/directories installs transient host storage policy. A successful reopen calls Self::load and replaces the entire current state; from_registry initializes both protection vectors empty and reopen restores neither. Pelt installs its appearance-store path only during EditorWindow::open, then uses shared native hooks, whose synchronization only refreshes font inventory/controls and export effects. Therefore a clean library reopen loses the actual caller guard and the exporter can accept the formerly protected appearance path. An existing file still triggers the ordinary explicit replacement prompt; it is no longer categorically refused as host-owned. The workshop own library/preferences path checks remain active. Current tests cover path aliases/replacement rechecks and reopen persistence separately, missing their composition.','diagnostics':['workshop_source_traces.json'],'repair_triage':{'disposition':'documented under active read-only audit goal','reason':'Preserve embedding policy/resource configuration across authored-library reload, or keep it in an owner that reload cannot replace. Add the actual protect/reopen/export composition case; broad state replacement should not erase host authority.'}},
 {'id':'Q329','title':'Shared workshop bindings replace the graph with a dirty leaf on every frame','source':'crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/src/preview_bindings.rs:66; crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/src/native_host.rs:73; crates/cambium/sprigging/src/glyphs.rs:198; crates/cambium/sprigging/src/lib.rs:401','status':'source-verified actual frame-to-registry-to-paint chain; native/GPU performance not measured','evidence':'The native frame hook invokes PreviewBindings::register every frame. Unlike its retained reader and stylesheet producers, register always leaves.insert(GRAPH_LEAF_KEY, Box::new(state.graph_leaf())). That creates a new GraphCanvas whose constructor sets dirty=true, replacing the prior leaf; render_into consequently repaints a visible graph even if state/size are unchanged. Its epoch and dependent retained-fragment work are invalidated on every such pass. The source tests verify shared geometry, colors and retained producer identity, not graph clean-frame reuse. This does not imply the wrapper continuously schedules redraws, nor quantify frame time/GPU cost. It is a concrete defeated cache gate in the maintained shared host binding.','diagnostics':['workshop_source_traces.json'],'repair_triage':{'disposition':'documented under active read-only audit goal','reason':'Retain the graph leaf and update it through invalidating setters only when its graph/theme/emphasis inputs change. Coordinate with Q325 public-style dirtiness; blindly mutating those fields would create a different stale-paint defect.'}}
]
for f in findings:f['verification']=NAME
