rows=[
 ('Workshop has one reusable model and two thin hosting bindings','Native and host-preview consumers use the same WorkshopState, view and PreviewBindings.', ['crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/src/lib.rs','crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/src/native_host.rs','crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/src/preview_bindings.rs'], 'Native owns focused-text/export/close routing; applications retain their event-loop, selected theme and exit policy. Pelt delegates those internals. The reviewed code supports this bounded shared-owner claim, not an independent implementation per host.'),
 ('Reloading authored state also replaces unrelated host policy','WorkshopState combines theme editing, preview sources, discovered fonts and protected export paths.', ['crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/src/state.rs','crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/src/interchange.rs','ports/pelt/desktop/appearance_editor.rs'], 'Q328 traces loss of the real Pelt host-file guard. Font inventory and preview source objects are also reset; native sync restores font discovery and retained bindings rebind current preview sources. Those repairs do not restore export policy.'),
 ('Saved choice has stronger checks than a dirty caption','saved_choice checks changes, pending name text, source kind, exact registry equality and valid presentation.', ['crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/src/state.rs','crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/tests/embedding_api.rs'], 'save builds candidate registry/draft and persists the library before publishing them. Session-only save says so. Initial blank/forked/imported state uses separate dirty and intake flags; do not equate every difference between is_dirty and has_changes with false persistence success.'),
 ('Export effects capture the draft before a host dialog','ExportArtifact owns format/name/contents while edits can continue.', ['crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/src/interchange.rs','crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/tests/interchange.rs'], 'CreateNew and explicit Replace use the shared Tabard atomic writer; path aliases and guarded directories are checked again before replacement. Export never clears the authored save point. These are shared mechanisms, but Q328 shows their policy inputs can be erased by reload.'),
 ('Path normalization is another implementation with a local purpose','Workshop resolves longest existing ancestors, missing suffixes and conservative case aliases.', ['crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/src/interchange.rs','crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/tests/interchange.rs'], 'Both canonical and lexical directory comparisons deliberately protect owned symlink entries. File protection checks canonical path equality rather than filesystem object IDs. Tests qualify Unix symlinks and Windows/macOS case variants separately; this source review did not run them.'),
 ('Preview isolation is real document/source separation','Reader and CSS specimens retain their own document/layout state; authored CSS is not installed into the workshop frame.', ['crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/src/reader.rs','crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/src/stylesheet.rs','crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/src/surface.rs'], 'Reader delegates extraction/lowering/layout to existing document components and preserves its Arc source across palette changes. The application fixture uses an independent real Livery document. Fixed semantic text is derived from source, rather than a duplicate manual paragraph.'),
 ('Typed preview fallback and authored CSS have explicitly different scope','Arbitrary CSS is shown in the isolated application specimen; reader/graph/syntax use seed-derived fallback.', ['crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/src/state.rs','crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/src/surface.rs'], 'The source clears mode sheets for typed fallback derivation and the UI states the distinction. A shared appearance workshop is not a promise that typed graph/reader paint interprets arbitrary CSS. Cache keys use seeds/harmony/mode and reattach typography/category data.'),
 ('Preview producer identity survives source replacement','Bindings retain SceneProducer objects, while set_source rebinds newly loaded WorkshopState preview Rc values.', ['crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/src/preview_bindings.rs','crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/tests/portable_capture.rs','crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/tests/shared_device_loss.rs'], 'Raster bases allocate two process-wide identities per binding. Leaf keys remain caller-host reserved constants; distinct bindings do not permit two full workshops sharing one local registry namespace. Device-loss tests explicitly qualify their distinct 701/702 leaf keys. Q329 is the exception to graph retention.'),
 ('Render refusal becomes blank scene data at the stylesheet specimen boundary','StylesheetSpecimen::frame returns Scene, saving a string diagnostic and creating an empty Scene on Livery error.', ['crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/src/stylesheet.rs','crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/src/preview_bindings.rs','crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/src/surface.rs'], 'SceneProducer sees an infallible frame callback, so it cannot propagate that failure as its typed producer error. The UI reads last_error through diagnostics on a later view build. No current Livery error was induced, and no claim that it is permanently invisible is made; investigate failure/rebuild/retry timing before repair.'),
 ('Typography controls represent two different preference owners','ThemeFontStyle edits authored theme family/size/line-height; FontRoleEditor stages application fallback stacks.', ['crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/src/typography.rs','crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/src/fonts.rs'], 'Similar role pickers and controlled text are repeated, but their persisted data/authority differ. The application editor preserves unedited ordered fallbacks; theme editor validates numbers and defers installed-family discovery to the host. FontRoleEditor::applied updates only baseline, so externally changed/normalized acknowledged preferences need consumer-specific reconciliation.'),
 ('Workshop header and pane report different dirty concepts','The header uses is_dirty while the pane uses has_changes.', ['crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/src/surface.rs','crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/src/state.rs'], 'Initial unsaved blank drafts may be dirty but closable; intake has a separate flag; pending name changes are synchronized by the ordinary message/native hook and explicit guards. save_and_close checks both after save. Existing source tests guard failed blank/import save cases; no fresh persistence run is claimed.'),
 ('Tinct owns palette math with intentional compatibility entry points','derive_palette_with uses explicit mode; legacy derive_palette uses Seeds.dark.', ['crates/cambium/tinct/src/lib.rs','crates/cambium/tinct/src/syntax.rs'], 'Explicit syntax profile gates every role at 4.5 or 7; legacy syntax preserves authored body/header and dim tiers. Tests assert the difference. The module broad contrast prose must be read with these function contracts; legacy author override is not automatically a new gate defect.'),
 ('Two contrast gates implement different algorithms','General UI roles mix RGB toward an extreme across bg/surface; syntax moves OKLCH lightness against one surface.', ['crates/cambium/tinct/src/gated.rs','crates/cambium/tinct/src/syntax.rs'], 'This is actual independent policy/math, not one helper under two names. General gate has explicit fallback after 50 steps and category 5 uses text_dim without another gate; syntax explicit mode has post-rail best-on/extreme fallback. Cross-role floor/alpha assumptions deserve tracing through consumers, not a universal guarantee from tests on selected palettes.'),
 ('Color conversion repeats sRGB linearization and mirrors external JS','Tinct has byte-channel and normalized-channel transfer implementations; gated.rs says it mirrors design-system tokens/tinct.js.', ['crates/cambium/tinct/src/lib.rs','crates/cambium/tinct/src/gated.rs'], 'The two Rust transfer functions use the same standard formula at different input scales. A fixed specimen test covers a few expected hexes; external JS source was not inspected and cross-language equivalence is unproven. color_to_hex drops alpha explicitly, contrast/luminance ignore it, while mix preserves its first input alpha.'),
 ('Native tests distinguish CPU mechanics, orderly recreation and actual destroy gates','Workshop test source covers routing, portable capture, headless GPU pixels and OS AX separately.', ['crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/tests/native_preview_render.rs','crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/tests/release_device_rehydration.rs','crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/tests/shared_device_loss.rs','crates/cambium/tabard-workshop/tests/os_accessibility/ax_probe.swift'], 'Ignored GPU boot failures fail instead of skip; delayed copies preserve original source and selected backgrounds. Orderly recreation does not claim forced driver loss; shared actual Device::destroy gate does not claim swapchain/physical driver reset. AX probe validates PID/executable, bounds work, and explicitly requires application receipts after OS delivery. All source read, none of these native/OS gates rerun this pass.'),
 ('Tinct original-suite pass is a bounded new receipt','All 23 current unit cases compile directly against one explicit retained serde variant.', ['crates/cambium/tinct/src/lib.rs','crates/cambium/tinct/src/gated.rs','crates/cambium/tinct/src/syntax.rs'], 'The first preflight found two retained serde feature variants and started no compiler/tests. Distinct v2 selects rc-enabled serde; all 23 original cases pass. No doctest, alpha compositing, external JS comparison, native consumer or fresh full supplier graph acceptance.'),
 ('Pelt scenario result is published before shared receipt export completes','EditorLane::complete stores outcome.ok in completion, which the embedding app reads.', ['ports/pelt/desktop/appearance_editor.rs','crates/cambium/mesquite/src/lane.rs'], 'This is another actual consumer of the completion-order seam identified earlier. Requested text receipt I/O can still fail after the callback. The parent consumer and CLI exit handling need tracing before calling it a false application exit; do not infer that completion=true overrides every lane error.')
]
